; Interprets: RFC 8581
;; What RFC 8581's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order. The document defines no command, and reprints RFC 7683's
;; OC-Supported-Features and OC-OLR with its own members, so a block here
;; is within one of them. Whether a node, or its peer, supports the
;; OC_PEER_REPORT feature, and what a request announced, neither the grouped
;; AVP's scope nor the answer alone shows, so a rule resting on them is
;; `text-only`.


;; The node's support of the feature.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: oc-feature-vector-peer-report-request
; AVP: OC-Feature-Vector
; Within: OC-Supported-Features
; Section: 6.1.1
"When sending a Diameter request, a DOIC node that supports the OC_PEER_REPORT feature (as defined in Section 7.1.1) MUST include in the OC-Supported-Features AVP an OC-Feature-Vector AVP with the OC_PEER_REPORT bit set."
    text-only


;; The node's support of the feature, and whose DiameterIdentity the
;; SourceID holds.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: oc-supported-features-source-id-request
; AVP: SourceID
; Within: OC-Supported-Features
; Section: 6.1.1
"When sending a request, a DOIC node that supports the OC_PEER_REPORT feature MUST include a SourceID AVP in the OC-Supported-Features AVP with its own DiameterIdentity."
    text-only
"When a Diameter Agent relays a request that includes a SourceID AVP in the OC-Supported-Features AVP, if the Diameter Agent supports the OC_PEER_REPORT feature, then it MUST remove the received SourceID AVP and replace it with a SourceID AVP containing its own DiameterIdentity."
    text-only


;; The peer's support, which the reporting node knows from the request.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: oc-feature-vector-peer-report-answer
; AVP: OC-Feature-Vector
; Within: OC-Supported-Features
; Section: 6.1.2
"If the peer supports the OC_PEER_REPORT feature, then the reporting node MUST indicate support for the feature in the OC-Supported-Features AVP."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: oc-supported-features-source-id-answer
; AVP: SourceID
; Within: OC-Supported-Features
; Section: 6.1.2
"When an agent relays an answer message, a reporting node that supports the OC_PEER_REPORT feature MUST strip any SourceID AVP from the OC-Supported-Features AVP."
    text-only
"If the peer supports the OC_PEER_REPORT feature, then the reporting node MUST insert the SourceID AVP in the OC-Supported-Features AVP in the answer message."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: oc-peer-algo-answer
; AVP: OC-Peer-Algo
; Within: OC-Supported-Features
; Section: 6.1.2
"If the peer supports the OC_PEER_REPORT feature, then the reporting node MUST insert the OC-Peer-Algo AVP in the OC-Supported-Features AVP. The OC-Peer-Algo AVP MUST indicate the overload abatement algorithm that the reporting node wants the reacting nodes to use should the reporting node send a Peer Overload report as a result of becoming overloaded."
    text-only


;; Section 6.2.4 is the reporting node's handling of a peer report: the
;; OC-OLR whose OC-Report-Type is PEER_REPORT (section 7.2.1). Whose
;; DiameterIdentity it holds is the sender's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: oc-olr-peer-report-source-id
; AVP: SourceID
; Within: OC-OLR
; Section: 6.2.4
"The reporting node MUST include its DiameterIdentity in the SourceID AVP in the OC-OLR AVP."
    present-if OC-Report-Type = PEER_REPORT


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: oc-olr-peer-report-agent-identity
; AVP: SourceID
; Within: OC-OLR
; Section: 7.2
"The peer report MUST also include the Diameter identity of the agent that generated the report."
"The SourceID AVP is used in the OC-OLR AVP to carry this DiameterIdentity."
    present-if OC-Report-Type = PEER_REPORT
